---
description: Status pill / status-badge styling convention (outline-only, never solid fill)
alwaysApply: true
---

# Status pills

Status pills (success / warning / error / info indicators that sit inline with text — "In progress", "Done", "Locked", "Short", etc.) MUST use the **outline** style:
white background, coloured text, 1.5px coloured border.

NEVER use solid-fill semantic backgrounds for pills (`var(--color-success-light)`,
`var(--color-warning-light)`, `var(--color-error-light)`, `var(--color-info-light)`).
Filled tints are reserved for full **banners**, **cards**, and **callout** rows
where the whole block is the message — not for inline pill-shaped status indicators.

## Canonical pill style

```tsx
<span
  style={{
    display: 'inline-flex',
    alignItems: 'center',
    gap: 5,
    padding: '3px 9px',
    borderRadius: 999,
    background: '#ffffff',
    color: 'var(--color-success)',           // or warning / error / info / text-secondary
    border: '1.5px solid var(--color-success)', // matches the colour above
    fontSize: 10,
    fontWeight: 700,
    textTransform: 'uppercase',
    letterSpacing: '0.05em',
    whiteSpace: 'nowrap',
  }}
>
  In progress
</span>
```

## Tone → border / text colour map

| Tone | text + border | Use for |
|---|---|---|
| `success` | `var(--color-success)` | done · ok · approved · in-progress |
| `warning` | `var(--color-warning)` | caution · pending · running long |
| `error`   | `var(--color-error)`   | failed · short · expired · variance |
| `info`    | `var(--color-info)`    | informational · linked · routed |
| `neutral` | `var(--color-text-secondary)` + border `var(--color-border)` | inactive / default state |

## Prefer the shared primitive

When adding a new pill, reach for the shared component first:

```tsx
import { StatusPill } from '@/components/ui/StatusPill';

<StatusPill tone="success">In progress</StatusPill>
```

Only roll a one-off span when the pill has bespoke layout requirements
(custom icon, embedded controls, etc.) — and even then, copy the canonical
style above, not a filled variant.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — solid fill semantic background
<span style={{
  background: 'var(--color-success-light)',
  color: 'var(--color-success)',
  borderRadius: 999,
  padding: '2px 8px',
  fontSize: 10,
  fontWeight: 700,
  textTransform: 'uppercase',
}}>In progress</span>

// ✅ GOOD — outline only
<span style={{
  background: '#ffffff',
  color: 'var(--color-success)',
  border: '1.5px solid var(--color-success)',
  borderRadius: 999,
  padding: '3px 9px',
  fontSize: 10,
  fontWeight: 700,
  textTransform: 'uppercase',
  letterSpacing: '0.05em',
}}>In progress</span>
```

## When you can keep a tinted background

Tinted `--color-*-light` backgrounds remain correct for:

- Full-width banners (`UrgentRemakeBanner`, `SpokeUrgentRemakeCard`)
- Callout cards / alert boxes spanning a row or column
- Table-row highlights for an exception state
- Icon containers (square/rounded tiles where the colour communicates the
  whole tile's meaning, not a status value next to text)

If in doubt: is this a *pill next to text*? → outline.
Is this a *block that frames its own message*? → tinted background is fine.
